{"parentUuid":"1eb0a272-6999-421a-9113-d6ee9c8231a6","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"c4acf1d5-04d7-4ac1-b8a0-93c2e1643196","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KYYp1DDFk9JJ5sJbc2hbEB","type":"tool_result","content":"--- name() and kind() in main.js\nweb/plan.js:80:  function nameOf(object) {\nweb/plan.js:83:    return link.method?.startsWith(\"procedural\") ? `${link.tag}?` : link.tag;\nweb/main.js:91:function kind(asset) {\nweb/main.js:98:function name(asset) {\nweb/main.js:101:  return link.method?.startsWith(\"procedural\") ? `${link.tag}?` : link.tag;\nfunction name(asset) {\n  const link = asset.mapping;\n  if (!link) return asset.label;\n  return link.method?.startsWith(\"procedural\") ? `${link.tag}?` : link.tag;\n}\n\nfunction addAsset(asset) {\n--- z-index and panel ids\n143:  z-index: 5;\n226:  z-index: 5;\n331:  z-index: 4;\n328-#plan {\n24:  <div id=\"hud\">\n25:    <div id=\"status\">Loading scene...</div>\n32:  <div id=\"buttons\">\n51:  <div id=\"info\" hidden>\n91:  <div id=\"add-panel\" hidden>\n116:  <div id=\"copilot\" hidden>\n117:    <button id=\"copilot-close\" aria-label=\"Close\">&times;</button>\n119:    <form id=\"copilot-form\">\n120:      <input id=\"copilot-input\" placeholder=\"Ask about the selecte\n123:    <div id=\"copilot-answer\"></div>\n--- click targets in the info panel\n55:    <button id=\"ask\" hidden>Ask copilot</button>\n56:    <button id=\"route-here\" hidden>Route here</button>\n57:    <button id=\"split-object\" hidden>Split into two</button>\n58:    <button id=\"combine-object\" hidden>Combine with...</button>\n59:    <button id=\"move\" hidden>Move on floor</button>\n--- does typing move the camera in the copilot?\nweb/main.js:468:  if (!phone.enabled && !busy) controls.update(camera);\n--- usage plan section\n## See the floor layout\nPress **Plan** for the room from above: walls, objects by type, the route, and an arrow showing where you are.\n- **Find:** type a tag or type, such as `P-005` or `tank`.\n- **Tap an object** to open its panel, then use **Route here**.\n- **Show pipes** adds pipes, which are hidden to keep it readable.\n- **Download DXF** saves the layout for CAD tools, with objects where they stand now.\n\n`make bim` writes an IFC model of the walls and objects for BIM tools, with each object's label and link in its\nproperties. Both are generated from the scan, not surveyed. Objects are boxes, and the scale hasn't been checked\non site. Without good evidence for a label, an object stays generic in the IFC. Needs `make api` and\n`Equipment Room.ply`.\n\n--- api docs\ndocs/USAGE.md:92:                      web/route.js: POST /api/changes, through web/serve.py to the \ndocs/USAGE.md:96:Route showing?        web/route.js: POST /api/route. While dragging it previews the\ndocs/USAGE.md:99:Reload the page       web/main.js: GET /api/assets, and restores saved moves on scr\ndocs/USAGE.md:100:Undo changes          web/route.js: POST /api/changes/reset\ndocs/PLAN.md:103:1. **Open (Benjamin):** load the scene, reduced if the tablet needs it, plus `GET /\ndocs/PLAN.md:104:2. **Details:** `GET /api/assets/{object_id}` joins the mapping, telemetry, alarms,\n--- how tests add an object\ntests/test_api.py:93:    added = client.post(\"/api/changes\", json={\"op\": \"add\", \"position\": [2, 1, 2]}).json()\ntests/test_api.py:96:        client.post(\"/api/changes\", json={\"op\": \"remove\", \"object_id\": \"near\"}).status_code == 200\ntests/test_select_object.py:129:    change = {\"op\": \"add\", \"position\": [0.5, 0.25, 1], \"details\": details}\ntests/test_select_object.py:140:    change = {\"op\": \"add\", \"position\": [0, 0, 0]}\napp/api/main.py:278:                raise HTTPException(503, \"Selecting needs the scene: set SCENE_P\n--- store statuses\n63:            asset.setdefault(\"status\", \"detected\")\n79:        return [a for a in self.assets.values() if a[\"status\"] not in GONE]\n119:            if asset is None or asset[\"status\"] in GONE:\n124:            if asset is None or asset[\"status\"] in GONE:\n129:            if asset is None or asset[\"status\"] in GONE:\n136:                asset[\"status\"] = \"removed\"\n155:            f\"new-{sum(a['status'] == 'new, unconfirmed' for a in self.assets.values()\n166:            \"status\": \"new, unconfirmed\",\n169:            # Only what an operator may set: identity and status never come from this.\n211:                \"status\": \"new, unconfirmed\",\n219:        parent[\"status\"] = \"split\"\n226:        if other is None or other[\"status\"] in GONE:\n--- real labels\n[('pipe', 154), ('object', 109), ('cart', 20), ('electrical cabinet', 19), ('box', 19), ('cable', 17), ('tank', 14), ('valve', 12), ('bag', 11), ('ladder', 9), ('bucket', 9), ('light fixture', 8), ('hose', 8), ('pipe fitting', 7), ('pump', 6), ('appliance', 4), ('tool', 4), ('shelf', 4), ('chair', 3), ('door', 1), ('sensor', 1), ('gauge', 1)]\nkeys ['scene_id', 'units', 'up', 'floor_height_along_up', 'floor_y', 'start']","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"ef9b6214-f399-492b-bb02-02654fc761b9","timestamp":"2026-11-07T12:51:18.291Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"--- name() and kind() in main.js\nweb/plan.js:80:  function nameOf(object) {\nweb/plan.js:83:    return link.method?.startsWith(\"procedural\") ? `${link.tag}?` : link.tag;\nweb/main.js:91:function kind(asset) {\nweb/main.js:98:function name(asset) {\nweb/main.js:101:  return link.method?.startsWith(\"procedural\") ? `${link.tag}?` : link.tag;\nfunction name(asset) {\n  const link = asset.mapping;\n  if (!link) return asset.label;\n  return link.method?.startsWith(\"procedural\") ? `${link.tag}?` : link.tag;\n}\n\nfunction addAsset(asset) {\n--- z-index and panel ids\n143:  z-index: 5;\n226:  z-index: 5;\n331:  z-index: 4;\n328-#plan {\n24:  <div id=\"hud\">\n25:    <div id=\"status\">Loading scene...</div>\n32:  <div id=\"buttons\">\n51:  <div id=\"info\" hidden>\n91:  <div id=\"add-panel\" hidden>\n116:  <div id=\"copilot\" hidden>\n117:    <button id=\"copilot-close\" aria-label=\"Close\">&times;</button>\n119:    <form id=\"copilot-form\">\n120:      <input id=\"copilot-input\" placeholder=\"Ask about the selecte\n123:    <div id=\"copilot-answer\"></div>\n--- click targets in the info panel\n55:    <button id=\"ask\" hidden>Ask copilot</button>\n56:    <button id=\"route-here\" hidden>Route here</button>\n57:    <button id=\"split-object\" hidden>Split into two</button>\n58:    <button id=\"combine-object\" hidden>Combine with...</button>\n59:    <button id=\"move\" hidden>Move on floor</button>\n--- does typing move the camera in the copilot?\nweb/main.js:468:  if (!phone.enabled && !busy) controls.update(camera);\n--- usage plan section\n## See the floor layout\nPress **Plan** for the room from above: walls, objects by type, the route, and an arrow showing where you are.\n- **Find:** type a tag or type, such as `P-005` or `tank`.\n- **Tap an object** to open its panel, then use **Route here**.\n- **Show pipes** adds pipes, which are hidden to keep it readable.\n- **Download DXF** saves the layout for CAD tools, with objects where they stand now.\n\n`make bim` writes an IFC model of the walls and objects for BIM tools, with each object's label and link in its\nproperties. Both are generated from the scan, not surveyed. Objects are boxes, and the scale hasn't been checked\non site. Without good evidence for a label, an object stays generic in the IFC. Needs `make api` and\n`Equipment Room.ply`.\n\n--- api docs\ndocs/USAGE.md:92:                      web/route.js: POST /api/changes, through web/serve.py to the \ndocs/USAGE.md:96:Route showing?        web/route.js: POST /api/route. While dragging it previews the\ndocs/USAGE.md:99:Reload the page       web/main.js: GET /api/assets, and restores saved moves on scr\ndocs/USAGE.md:100:Undo changes          web/route.js: POST /api/changes/reset\ndocs/PLAN.md:103:1. **Open (Benjamin):** load the scene, reduced if the tablet needs it, plus `GET /\ndocs/PLAN.md:104:2. **Details:** `GET /api/assets/{object_id}` joins the mapping, telemetry, alarms,\n--- how tests add an object\ntests/test_api.py:93:    added = client.post(\"/api/changes\", json={\"op\": \"add\", \"position\": [2, 1, 2]}).json()\ntests/test_api.py:96:        client.post(\"/api/changes\", json={\"op\": \"remove\", \"object_id\": \"near\"}).status_code == 200\ntests/test_select_object.py:129:    change = {\"op\": \"add\", \"position\": [0.5, 0.25, 1], \"details\": details}\ntests/test_select_object.py:140:    change = {\"op\": \"add\", \"position\": [0, 0, 0]}\napp/api/main.py:278:                raise HTTPException(503, \"Selecting needs the scene: set SCENE_P\n--- store statuses\n63:            asset.setdefault(\"status\", \"detected\")\n79:        return [a for a in self.assets.values() if a[\"status\"] not in GONE]\n119:            if asset is None or asset[\"status\"] in GONE:\n124:            if asset is None or asset[\"status\"] in GONE:\n129:            if asset is None or asset[\"status\"] in GONE:\n136:                asset[\"status\"] = \"removed\"\n155:            f\"new-{sum(a['status'] == 'new, unconfirmed' for a in self.assets.values()\n166:            \"status\": \"new, unconfirmed\",\n169:            # Only what an operator may set: identity and status never come from this.\n211:                \"status\": \"new, unconfirmed\",\n219:        parent[\"status\"] = \"split\"\n226:        if other is None or other[\"status\"] in GONE:\n--- real labels\n[('pipe', 154), ('object', 109), ('cart', 20), ('electrical cabinet', 19), ('box', 19), ('cable', 17), ('tank', 14), ('valve', 12), ('bag', 11), ('ladder', 9), ('bucket', 9), ('light fixture', 8), ('hose', 8), ('pipe fitting', 7), ('pump', 6), ('appliance', 4), ('tool', 4), ('shelf', 4), ('chair', 3), ('door', 1), ('sensor', 1), ('gauge', 1)]\nkeys ['scene_id', 'units', 'up', 'floor_height_along_up', 'floor_y', 'start']","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputEx