{"parentUuid":"d70032c1-45a4-46c7-a61b-6d2651d47b03","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgocYMk8LDws9FTAk899F","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016byGm7qmQoL28b6WRXRwCb","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies; S=/tmp/claude-1000/-home-viktor-trilar-Projects-Newbies/6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028/scratchpad; uv tree --frozen --invert --package pillow --depth 1 2>/dev/null | head -8 | cut -c1-70; python3 - <<'EOF'\ndef patch(path, pairs):\n    text = open(path).read()\n    for old, new in pairs:\n        assert old in text, (path, old[:70])\n        text = text.replace(old, new, 1)\n    open(path, \"w\").write(text)\npatch(\"app/plan/layout.py\", [\n(\"\"\"import numpy as np\nfrom PIL import Image\nfrom scipy import ndimage\n\"\"\", \"\"\"from typing import Any\n\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy import ndimage\n\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\") -> tuple[Image.Image, dict]:\n\"\"\", \"\"\") -> tuple[Any, dict]:\n\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"    first, second, axis, sign = plan_axes(up)\n    positions = splats.positions.astype(np.float64)\n\"\"\", \"\"\"    from PIL import Image\n\n    first, second, axis, sign = plan_axes(up)\n    positions = splats.positions.astype(np.float64)\n\"\"\"),\n])\npath = \"docs/RESULTS.md\"; text = open(path).read()\nmarker = \"| 2026-11-07 | Viktor | Shape fit: reject cylinders\"\nassert marker in text\nrows = (\n\"| 2026-11-07 | Viktor | Floor layout and DXF (`app/plan`) | `Equipment Room.ply`, objects-v2, 440 objects, 30 links | Walls from `estimate_room`, 2.5 cm per pixel | Image 389 x 315 px in 0.63 s. Room 9.12 x 7.27 m, the same as BIM mode. DXF: 1,764 lines, 30 tags and a not-surveyed note, reads back in ezdxf. All 30 tags show as guesses, such as `P-005?` | About 1 s | Not measured | ThinkPad |\\n\"\n\"| 2026-11-07 | Viktor | Wall estimates compared | `Equipment Room.ply` | Sasha's scan density bands against my occupancy profiles, found independently | Agree within 5.3 cm on every side (1.7, 0, 5.3 and 2.8 cm). Mine was dropped so that the room has one size everywhere. Neither is checked on site | | | ThinkPad |\\n\"\n\"| 2026-11-07 | Viktor | IFC download with operator changes (`/api/plan/model.ifc`) | Same, after dragging `obj-0067` to (-1.46, -1.75) in a headless browser | Sasha's writer on the backend's current objects | 445 elements, 0 IfcOpenShell schema issues, the cart is at (-1.46, -1.75). The DXF from the same session changed by exactly the cart's 4 lines | | | ThinkPad |\\n\"\n)\nopen(path, \"w\").write(text.replace(marker, rows + marker, 1))\nopen(\"handoffs/viktortrilar.md\", \"w\").write(\"\"\"# viktortrilar: viktor/bim\n**Goal:** the bird's-eye floor layout Alpo asked for, a DXF export, and an IFC download that includes operator changes, on top of Sasha's BIM mode\n**Done:** app/plan/ (floor image, DXF), web/plan.js and the Plan button, /api/plan routes including live /api/plan/model.ifc. Walls now come from Sasha's `estimate_room`, and my own IFC export is gone. web/serve.py forwards file types and names. The button row wraps instead of sliding off narrow screens. Guessed links read `P-005?` everywhere\n**Verified:** 231 tests passed, 2 skipped, lint clean. Headless browser on real data: Plan, search, tap, move, real DXF and IFC downloads, no page errors. Read back: the DXF changed by exactly the cart's 4 lines, the IFC has 0 schema issues with the cart at its new spot. Not tested: a real BIM or CAD tool, 5090, tablet\n**Next:** PR #26 (Sasha's BIM mode plus fixes) needs merging first, then this PR. Then rehearse on the 5090\n**Blockers:** merging needs Viktor's word: the permission system refused my merge of #26. An agent is fixing routes that ignore moved objects on `viktor/route-keeps-moved-objects`, not finished. Roihu closed until at least Monday. Local branch viktor/viewer-objects holds an unused merge: don't merge it\n\"\"\")\nEOF\nuv run --only-group dev ruff format --check . 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-80; make lint 2>&1 | grep -E \"^[A-Z][0-9]+ |All checks passed|would be\" | cut -c1-90; uv run --no-project --with numpy --with scipy --with pandas --with openpyxl --with pytest --with fastapi --with httpx --with pillow --with 'psycopg[binary]' --with ifcopenshell --with ezdxf pytest -q 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-90; echo \"--- API loads without Pillow\"; uv run --no-project --isolated --with numpy --with scipy --with fastapi --with pydantic --with openpyxl --with pandas --with 'psycopg[binary]' python -c \"import app.api.main; print('API imports fine without Pillow')\" 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-110; echo \"--- commit as one\"; git add README.md app/api/main.py app/bim/ifc.py app/bim/model.py app/plan docs/RESULTS.md docs/USAGE.md handoffs/viktortrilar.md tests/test_plan.py web/bim.js web/index.html web/main.js web/plan.js web/serve.py web/style.css; git status --short | grep -v \"^[AMD] \" | cut -c1-60; git reset -q --soft viktor/bim-model-fixes && git commit -q -m \"Add a Plan screen, a DXF export, and an IFC download with operator changes\n\nPlan shows the room from above with objects, the route and where you are, as\nAlpo asked for. Download DXF and Download IFC both show objects as they stand\nnow. Walls come from the BIM model's room estimate, so the room has one size.\n\nAlso fixes what this ran into: the viewer's proxy dropped file types and names,\nthe button row slid off narrow screens, and P-005 read as confirmed in the\nviewer although it isn't.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\"; git log --format='%h %an %s' -2 | cut -c1-90; git show --stat --format= HEAD | tail -18 | cut -c1-70","description":"Make Pillow optional at import, record results, test, and commit","timeout":300000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2530,"cache_read_input_tokens":326496,"output_tokens":3183,"output