{"parentUuid":"8e2f98c8-10e9-480a-b3e2-93d175b4c89e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgochT95aYjLJUThSJ9DE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NUmUKmwx2EYN9jhi8icUtp","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies; S=/tmp/claude-1000/-home-viktor-trilar-Projects-Newbies/6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028/scratchpad; git fetch origin 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-80; echo \"main moved by: $(git rev-list --count viktor/bim-model-fixes..origin/main)\"; git push -q git@github.com:Sairanyx/Newbies.git viktor/bim 2>&1 | grep -v \"^remote:\" | tail -3 | cut -c1-120; cat > \"$S/pr2.md\" <<'EOF'\n**Merge #26 first.** This is stacked on it, so the diff shows only this work. Once #26 is in, change this PR's base to `main`.\n\nAdds the bird's-eye layout Alpo asked for (\"It gives bird eye view\"), plus exports that show objects as they stand now. BIM isn't in the weighted scoring, so this is a nice-to-have.\n\n**Plan screen:**\n- Shows the room from above with walls, objects by type, the route, and an arrow for where you are.\n- Search by tag or type: `P-005` highlights one object, `tank` highlights all 14.\n- Tapping an object opens its panel, so **Route here** and **Ask copilot** work from there.\n- Colours match BIM mode, and a dashed outline means the object can be moved.\n\n**Exports:**\n- **Download DXF** (new): `/api/plan/layout.dxf`, with walls, footprints on layers by type, and tags.\n- **Download IFC** (now live): with the backend running, it comes from `/api/plan/model.ifc` and includes moved, split, combined, added and removed objects. Without a backend, you still get the file `make bim` built.\n\n**Shared room estimate:** the Plan screen now uses `estimate_room` from `app/bim`, so the room is 9.12 x 7.27 m everywhere. My own wall fit agreed with it within 5.3 cm on every side, and I removed it along with my IFC export.\n\n**Bugs fixed along the way:**\n- `web/serve.py` sent everything as JSON and dropped file names.\n- The bottom button row slid off the left edge on tablet-width screens once a route was showing, hiding **Go to P-005**, **Copilot** and **Plan**. It now wraps.\n- Typing in the Plan search box no longer moves the camera. The same problem may still exist in the copilot's text box, which this doesn't touch.\n\n**Visible change in the viewer:** P-005 now reads `P-005?` in labels and panels, because its link is an unconfirmed pick by eye. The panel for it still shows `manual_visual_unconfirmed, confidence 0.3`. The **Go to P-005** button keeps its name.\n\n**Tested:**\n- 231 tests passed, 2 skipped, lint clean. CI only installs the dev tools, so its tests that need numpy are skipped; these ran locally with ezdxf and IfcOpenShell.\n- Headless browser on the real scene: search, tap, the panel opening on top of the Plan screen, handing over to the 3D view for a move, real DXF and IFC downloads, all buttons on screen at 1024 and 800 px wide, no page errors.\n- Read back after dragging the cart to (-1.46, -1.75): the DXF changed by exactly the cart's 4 lines, and the IFC has 0 schema issues with the cart at that spot.\n\n**Not tested:** opening the files in a real CAD or BIM tool, the 5090, a tablet. Rotation from Eduard's branch isn't handled: once it merges, footprints, BIM boxes and exports will follow an object's position but not its turn.\n\n**Conflicts to expect:** `web/main.js`, `web/index.html` and `web/style.css` overlap with the unmerged tablet work on `eduard` and `benjamin/webviewer`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nEOF\ngh pr create --base viktor/bim-model-fixes --head viktor/bim --title \"Add a Plan screen, a DXF export, and an IFC download with operator changes\" --body-file \"$S/pr2.md\" 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-100; gh pr list --state open --json number,headRefName,baseRefName --jq '.[] | \"#\\(.number) \\(.headRefName) -> \\(.baseRefName)\"'; echo \"--- trial: both PRs on today's main, against the teammates' branches\"; for b in origin/eduard origin/benjamin/webviewer; do echo \"[$b + viktor/bim]\"; git merge-tree --write-tree --name-only \"$b\" viktor/bim 2>&1 | sed -n '2,/^$/p' | grep -v '^$' | head -12 | cut -c1-60 | tr '\\n' ' '; echo; done; git worktree list | cut -c1-110; git status -sb | head -2 | cut -c1-70","description":"Push my branch, open the stacked pull request, and check conflicts","timeout":120000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3786,"cache_read_input_tokens":329026,"output_tokens":2106,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":263},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3786,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2106,"cache_read_input_tokens":329026,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3786,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3786},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":14917,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01NUmUKmwx2EYN9jhi8icUtp":{"command":"cd /home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies; S=/tmp/claude-1000/-home-viktor-trilar-Projects-Newbies/6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028/scratchpad; git fetch origin 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-80; echo \"main moved by: $(git rev-list --count viktor/bim-model-fixes..origin/main)\"; git push -q git@github.com:Sairanyx/Newbies.git viktor/bim 2>&1 | grep -v \"^remote:\" | tail -3 | cut -c1-120; cat > \"$S/pr2.md\" <<'EOF'\n**Merge #26 first.** This is stacked on it, so the diff shows only this work. Once #26 is in, change this PR's base to `main`.\n\nAdds the bird's-eye layout Alpo asked for (\"It gives bird eye view\"), plus exports that