{"parentUuid":"f585dd77-8f7f-4084-8da8-ce028a346754","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"caa08ac3-2937-47f3-a14c-5ddd43c038da","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017dQ9cu3iCuK1FR5EHRdbWH","type":"tool_result","content":"--- all tests\n-- Docs: https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/how-to/capture-warnings.html\n219 passed, 19 skipped, 1 warning in 11.79s\n--- lint\nAll checks passed!\n--- how the browser checks run\n4096 main_copy\n5898240 main.tar\n2686 old_spot.py\n4749 patch_eduard.py\n4096 __pycache__\n1290 refusal_map.py\n4096 reload_cwd\n2321 reload.log\n2132 reload_test.sh\n3197 repro.py\n502 serve_on_port.py\n1608 shot.py\n13105 verify.py\n4096 watch\n\"\"\"Everything the fix has to hold for, through the real viewer with real pointer events.\n\n    verify.py SCRIPTS_DIR WATCH_DIR [view]\n\"\"\"\nimport json\nimport pathlib\nimport sys\nimport time\n\nsys.path.insert(0, sys.argv[1])\nfrom harness import CHAIR, Run, start  # noqa: E402\n\nWATCH = pathlib.Path(sys.argv[2])\nVIEW = sys.argv[3] if len(sys.argv) > 3 else \"objects\"\nOUT = pathlib.Path(sys.argv[1])\nCLEAR = 0.25  # metres: the planner keeps 0.3 from a box, less grid rounding\nCART = \"obj-0067\"\nGOOD = (-0.6, -1.45)  # on the straight route to P-005\nREFUSED = (-1.7, -1.3)  # in the cart's area\n\nplaywright = start()\nrun = Run(playwright, view=VIEW if VIEW != \"scan\" else \"\")\nrun.page.evaluate(\"() => { window.__h.look(-0.7); }\")\nresults = []\n\n\ndef check(name, ok, detail=\"\"):\n    results.append((name, bool(ok)))\n    print(f\"  {'pass' if ok else 'FAIL'}  {name}  {detail}\", flush=True)\n\n10:sys.path.insert(0, sys.argv[1])\n13:WATCH = pathlib.Path(sys.argv[2])\n14:VIEW = sys.argv[3] if len(sys.argv) > 3 else \"objects\"\n15:OUT = pathlib.Path(sys.argv[1])\n--- USAGE and RESULTS\n+| 2026-11-07 | Viktor | Moved chair keeps blocking routes | `obj-0021`, route to P-005, real pointer drags in a headless browser, 9 checks | A clean drop, a drop on a refused spot, then a clean drop, moving th\n-| \"Couldn't save the move\" | The backend refused it or is down | The message says why. Restart `make api` if needed |\n+| \"Couldn't save the move, so it went back\" | The backend refused it, so the object returned to where the backend has it | The message says why. Try another spot |\n+| \"Couldn't save the change, trying again\" | The backend can't be reached. Routes ignore the change until it's saved | Start `make api`. The viewer sends it once it's back |\n-| Everything is back after reloading the backend | No database | Run `make db` before `make api` |\n+| \"The backend lost saved moves\" | `make api` restarted with no database, which it does whenever a `.py` file in the repo changes. Or someone pressed **Undo changes** on another screen | Run `make db` before `\n+\n+\n+def test_route_says_how_many_changes_the_backend_holds(tmp_path):\n+    \"\"\"The viewer compares this with what it sent, to notice a backend that has lost its moves.\"\"\"\n+    assets = [box(\"target\", [5.5, -0.5, 1.0], \"fixed\"), box(\"cart\", [0.6, -0.5, 1.0], \"movable\")]\n+    path = tmp_path / \"assets.json\"\n+    path.write_text(json.dumps({\"scene_id\": \"t\", \"assets\": assets}))\n+    client = TestClient(create_app(path, open_floor(tmp_path), database=FakeDatabase()))\n+    request = {\"start\": [2.0, 0.0, 1.0], \"object_id\": \"target\"}\n+    assert client.post(\"/api/route\", json=request).json()[\"changes\"] == 0\n+    move = {\"op\": \"move\", \"object_id\": \"cart\", \"position\": [0.6, -0.5, 1.5]}\n+    assert client.post(\"/api/changes\", json=move).json()[\"change_id\"] == 1\n+    assert client.post(\"/api/route\", json=request).json()[\"changes\"] == 1\n+    client.post(\"/api/changes/reset\")\n+    assert client.post(\"/api/route\", json=request).json()[\"changes\"] == 0\n+\n+\n+def test_placeholder_route_says_how_many_changes_the_backend_holds(client):\n+    request = {\"start\": [0, 0, 0], \"object_id\": \"near\"}\n+    assert client.post(\"/api/route\", json=request).json()[\"changes\"] == 0\n# viktortrilar: viktor/route-keeps-moved-objects\n**Goal:** a moved object must keep blocking routes after the viewer or person moves. The black chair (`obj-0021`) was ignored\n**Done:** \"last good spot\" is now a spot that was really checked (`web/objects.js`). A refused move goes back on screen and routes re-plan. A save that can't get through is retried. The viewer follows a backend that lost its moves (`web/route.js`, `web/main.js\n**Verified:** on main 5c65da2: lint; 219 tests passed, 19 skipped (no torch or Excel pack here). Headless browser, real pointer drags on real data: 66 of 66 checks, covering the viewer moving, walking the route, Fly, undo, reload, forced refusal, failed save, \n**Next:** open a PR. Merge with Eduard's branch: keep this `saveChanges`, remember the checked yaw in `showCheck`, and stop rounding in `recordChange`\n**Blockers:** a moved chair's old spot still isn't walkable: its second box `obj-0090` stays there, and the floor map has specks of unlabelled chair splats (pre-existing). `make api` restarts on any `.py` edit under the repo, including `.claude/worktrees/`, an","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"00007731-489c-4d35-ad73-0b466ecb01e2","timestamp":"2026-11-07T13:43:57.616Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"--- all tests\n-- Docs: https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/how-to/capture-warnings.html\n219 passed, 19 skipped, 1 warning in 11.79s\n--- lint\nAll checks passed!\n--- how the browser checks run\n4096 main_copy\n5898240 main.tar\n2686 old_spot.py\n4749 patch_eduard.py\n4096 __pycache__\n1290 refusal_map.py\n4096 reload_cwd\n2321 reload.log\n2132 reload_test.sh\n3197 repro.py\n502 serve_on_port.py\n1608 shot.py\n13105 verify.py\n4096 watch\n\"\"\"Everything the fix has to hold for, through the real viewer with real pointer events.\n\n    verify.py SCRIPTS_DIR WATCH_DIR [view]\n\"\"\"\nimport json\nimport pathlib\nimport sys\nimport time\n\nsys.path.insert(0, sys.argv[1])\nfrom h