t sent, to notice a backend that has lost its moves.\"\"\"\n+    assets = [box(\"target\", [5.5, -0.5, 1.0], \"fixed\"), box(\"cart\", [0.6, -0.5, 1.0], \"movable\")]\n+    path = tmp_path / \"assets.json\"\n+    path.write_text(json.dumps({\"scene_id\": \"t\", \"assets\": assets}))\n+    client = TestClient(create_app(path, open_floor(tmp_path), database=FakeDatabase()))\n+    request = {\"start\": [2.0, 0.0, 1.0], \"object_id\": \"target\"}\n+    assert client.post(\"/api/route\", json=request).json()[\"changes\"] == 0\n+    move = {\"op\": \"move\", \"object_id\": \"cart\", \"position\": [0.6, -0.5, 1.5]}\n+    assert client.post(\"/api/changes\", json=move).json()[\"change_id\"] == 1\n+    assert client.post(\"/api/route\", json=request).json()[\"changes\"] == 1\n+    client.post(\"/api/changes/reset\")\n+    assert client.post(\"/api/route\", json=request).json()[\"changes\"] == 0\n+\n+\n+def test_placeholder_route_says_how_many_changes_the_backend_holds(client):\n+    request = {\"start\": [0, 0, 0], \"object_id\": \"near\"}\n+    assert client.post(\"/api/route\", json=request).json()[\"changes\"] == 0\n# viktortrilar: viktor/route-keeps-moved-objects\n**Goal:** a moved object must keep blocking routes after the viewer or person moves. The black chair (`obj-0021`) was ignored\n**Done:** \"last good spot\" is now a spot that was really checked (`web/objects.js`). A refused move goes back on screen and routes re-plan. A save that can't get through is retried. The viewer follows a backend that lost its moves (`web/route.js`, `web/main.js\n**Verified:** on main 5c65da2: lint; 219 tests passed, 19 skipped (no torch or Excel pack here). Headless browser, real pointer drags on real data: 66 of 66 checks, covering the viewer moving, walking the route, Fly, undo, reload, forced refusal, failed save, \n**Next:** open a PR. Merge with Eduard's branch: keep this `saveChanges`, remember the checked yaw in `showCheck`, and stop rounding in `recordChange`\n**Blockers:** a moved chair's old spot still isn't walkable: its second box `obj-0090` stays there, and the floor map has specks of unlabelled chair splats (pre-existing). `make api` restarts on any `.py` edit under the repo, including `.claude/worktrees/`, an","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"b662f425-7cca-404e-9067-5aca1a8236e0","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","root":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Sairanyx/Newbies","visibility":"unknown"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Sairanyx/Newbies","visibility":"unknown"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Sairanyx/Newbies","visibility":"unknown"}]}},"live_cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","platform":"linux"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f585dd77-8f7f-4084-8da8-ce028a346754","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies/.claude/worktrees/agent-aef4b903dc16194fa","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"main","slug":"vast-jumping-lobster"}
