{"parentUuid":"6666b120-4b34-4702-880f-0c5b1c8a5206","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgofxoWCx3YsAfHqL9oT7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**The chair bug is fixed, on a local branch that isn't pushed yet (`viktor/route-keeps-moved-objects`).** I reran the agent's browser checks on its final commit, which sits on the latest main: 66 of 66 pass with no page errors. Lint is clean and 219 tests pass. The other 19 are skipped because that copy of the repo has no torch or Excel pack.\n\n## What was going wrong\nThe chair is refused on about half the floor (381 of 743 spots, by the agent's count). Dragging it across one of those spots wrongly recorded that spot as its \"last good spot\":\n1. **On release:** the chair stayed there on screen, but the backend refused the move.\n2. **Saving:** the refused move then blocked every later move from saving.\n3. **Routes:** during the drag the route looked right, because previews send the chair's position with each request. Once you moved, routes used the backend's old position and went straight through the chair.\n\nNow only a spot that passed the check counts as good. A refused drop sends the chair back with a message, and later moves still save.\n\n**A second cause looks the same:** `make api` restarts whenever a `.py` file in the repo changes, including in agent worktrees, and forgets moves unless `make db` is running. The viewer now notices, moves objects back and warns you, but the restart still happens. I can't tell which of the two you hit.\n\n## Eduard's commit doesn't replace this\nEduard's `7e60da7` only fixes the blocked saves. This is the agent's comparison; I didn't rerun it:\n\n| Build | Checks passed | After a refused drop | Next clean move |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Main before the fix | 3 of 9 | Route hits the chair | Route hits the chair |\n| Eduard's branch | 6 of 9 | Route hits the chair | Fine |\n| This fix | 9 of 9 | Clear by at least 0.31 m | Clear by at least 0.27 m |\n| Eduard's branch + this fix | 9 of 9 | Clear by at least 0.30 m | Clear by at least 0.27 m |\n\nMerging will add conflicts with Eduard's branch in `web/route.js`, `web/objects.js` and `tests/test_api.py`. The agent tested a resolved version on Eduard's code, but not a real merge with main.\n\n## Still not solved\n- **Moving an object away often doesn't open a path:** this was already the case. The chair's old spot stays blocked because its second box, `obj-0090`, stays behind and the floor map still holds some of its splats. The agent measured that 47% of movable objects have under half their floor free in the map. In the demo, show a route bending around a moved object, not one opening up.\n- **Restarts are only reported:** for the demo, run `make db` and don't edit code on that machine.\n- **Rare case:** if Undo fails while the backend is down and someone moves an object before it's back, the reset is skipped.\n- **No repo test for the viewer part:** the browser checks live in the scratchpad, so nothing in the repo guards this part of the fix.\n- **Not tested:** `make check` itself, the 5090, a tablet or touch, or a restart with a real database.\n\nMain also moved while this ran: Sasha merged #28, which adds Real/Mesh/Box looks to BIM mode. The fix sits on top of it, but I haven't retested Plan or the exports since.\n\n**Should I push this, open the PR and merge it?** I'd also limit `make api`'s auto-restart to `app/`, a one-line change, so edits in agent worktrees can't wipe moves mid-demo."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3018,"cache_read_input_tokens":374315,"output_tokens":5172,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3992},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3018,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5172,"cache_read_input_tokens":374315,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3018,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3018},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"f4f416e6-1b78-4ed0-99f7-de7a4025e29a","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgofxnrkS8iUf9VZMj5XA","requestRef":"0d4a9089-9acc-4188-a789-efb6f777b58d","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"e9de331f-fdbb-4f78-9e02-387978d6a524","timestamp":"2026-11-07T13:48:57.231Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies/.claude/worktrees/agent-aef4b903dc16194fa","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"main","slug":"vast-jumping-lobster"}
