{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","id":"3293e839-5041-4e8e-a082-381b187c18bf","timestamp":"2026-11-07T13:58:35.091Z","version":"2.1.319","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"722db4f18cedb330133d1505341dd7fba4dc656fa048fe0f251a9d2ff7e226fc","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"faa0e256-9367-405a-b7fb-befa408446c6","keep":123,"tail":["91d7f2cb695afcf074cd08ba3499eeeb493e72a86d3ea5dcef5f29289dfbf153","a14e255fefc0a5c531637609f9281437df5c3b158f57d0b038ef652024e7b157"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",124,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"0a378e2e6f0c0cc09c3db185d34d904dfcc2784056b9db704a73b42db142c9e3"}
{"parentUuid":"3218e348-9e6b-4609-872f-a00e8608b46a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgogkxtY9UTiwxnFz1T6P","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Wg2Q1QR13MFnppgfwWBfsd","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"W=/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies/.claude/worktrees/agent-aef4b903dc16194fa; S=/tmp/claude-1000/-home-viktor-trilar-Projects-Newbies/6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028/scratchpad; cd \"$W\"; git push -q git@github.com:Sairanyx/Newbies.git viktor/route-keeps-moved-objects 2>&1 | grep -v \"^remote:\" | tail -2 | cut -c1-100; cat > \"$S/pr3.md\" <<'EOF'\nFixes routes going through a moved object once the viewer moves, reported with the black chair (`obj-0021`).\n\n**Cause:** dragging across a refused spot recorded it as the \"last good spot\". On release the viewer kept showing the object there while the backend refused the move, and the refused move then blocked every later save. Previews send the position with each request, so the route looked right until the viewer moved.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Only a spot that passed the check counts as good, and that exact spot is saved.\n- A refused drop goes back on screen with a message, and later moves still save.\n- A save that can't get through is retried every 2 s.\n- Route replies carry a change count, so the viewer notices a backend that lost its moves (a restart without `make db`, or Undo on another screen), follows it, and warns for 8 s.\n\n**Tested:**\n- 66 of 66 browser checks with real pointer drags on real data, rerun on the final commit, no page errors. They cover the viewer moving, walking the route, Fly, undo, reload, refusals, failed saves and an API restart. The scripts are in a local scratch folder, not this repo.\n- Lint clean, 219 tests passed, 19 skipped locally.\n\n**Not tested:** `make check` itself, the 5090, a tablet or touch, a restart with a real database.\n\n**Known gaps:**\n- A moved object's old spot can stay blocked, as before: the chair's second box `obj-0090` stays behind, and the floor map holds some of its splats.\n- If Undo fails while the backend is down and someone moves an object before it's back, the reset is skipped.\n\n**Eduard:** `7e60da7` fixes the blocked saves but not the refused drop. This uses the same queue shape, but expect conflicts in `web/route.js`, `web/objects.js` and `tests/test_api.py`. Keep this `saveChanges`, remember the checked yaw alongside the spot in `showCheck`, and stop rounding in `recordChange`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nEOF\ngh pr create --base main --head viktor/route-keeps-moved-objects --title \"Keep moved objects blocking routes once the viewer moves\" --body-file \"$S/pr3.md\" 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-90; N=$(gh pr view viktor/route-keeps-moved-objects --json number --jq .number); sleep 8; timeout 200 gh pr checks \"$N\" --watch --interval 10 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-90; gh pr view \"$N\" --json mergeable,mergeStateStatus --jq '\"#'$N' \\(.mergeable) \\(.mergeStateStatus)\"'","description":"Push the route fix, open its pull request and wait for CI","timeout":280000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1015,"cache_read_input_tokens":382590,"output_tokens":1215,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1015,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1215,"cache_read_input_tokens":382590,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1015,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1015},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":9704,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Wg2Q1QR13MFnppgfwWBfsd":{"command":"W=/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies/.claude/worktrees/agent-aef4b903dc16194fa; S=/tmp/claude-1000/-home-viktor-trilar-Projects-Newbies/6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028/scratchpad; cd \"$W\"; git push -q git@github.com:Sairanyx/Newbies.git viktor/route-keeps-moved-objects 2>&1 | grep -v \"^remote:\" | tail -2 | cut -c1-100; cat > \"$S/pr3.md\" <<'EOF'\nFixes routes going through a moved object once the viewer moves, reported with the black chair (`obj-0021`).\n\n**Cause:** dragging across a refused spot recorded it as the \"last good spot\". On release the viewer kept showing the object there while the backend refused the move, and the refused move then blocked every later save. Previews send the position with each request, so the route looked right until the viewer moved.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Only a spot that passed the check counts as good, and that exact spot is saved.\n- A refused drop goes back on screen with a message, and later moves still save.\n- A save that can't get through is retried every 2 s.\n- Route replies carry a change count, so the viewer notices a backend that lost its moves (a restart without `make db`, or Undo on another screen), follows it, and warns for 8 s.\n\n**Tested:**\n- 66 of 66 browser checks with real pointer drags on real data, rerun on the final commit, no page errors. They cover the viewer moving, walking the route, Fly, undo, reload, refusals, failed saves and an API restart. The scripts are in a local scratch folder, not this repo.\n- Lint clean, 219 tests passed, 19 skipped locally.\n\n**Not tested:** `make check` itself, the 5090, a tablet or touch, a restart with a real database.\n\n**Known gaps:**\n- A moved object's old spot can stay blocked, as before: the chair's second box `obj-0090` stays behind, and the floor map holds some of its splats.\n- If Undo fails while the backend is down and someone moves an object before it's back, the reset is skipped.\n\n**Eduard:** `7e60da7` fixes the blocked saves but not the refused drop. This uses the same queue shape, but expect conflicts in `web/route.js`, `web/objects.js` and `tests/test_api.py`. Keep this `saveChanges`, remember the checked yaw alongside the spot in `showCheck`, and stop rounding in `recordChange`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nEOF\ngh pr create --base main --head viktor/route-keeps-moved-objects --title \"Keep moved objects blocking routes once the viewer moves\" --body-file \"$S/pr3.md\" 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-90; N=$(gh pr view viktor/route-keeps-moved-objects --json number --jq .number); sleep 8; timeout 200 gh pr checks \"$N\" --watch --interval 10 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-90; gh pr view \"$N\" --json mergeable,mergeStateStatus --jq '\"#'$N' \\(.mergeable) \\(.mergeStateStatus)\"'","description":"Push the route fix, open its pull request and wait for CI","timeout":280000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"2391c503-3f4f-4a3a-8ab4-5c7901a83917","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgogkxcucc2umiv7TraGe","requestRef":"3293e839-5041-4e8e-a082-381b187c18bf","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"81b988aa-7c43-4333-9c3a-bf8a1f34614a","timestamp":"2026-11-07T13:58:45.630Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies/.claude/worktrees/agent-aef4b903dc16194fa","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"main","slug":"vast-jumping-lobster"}
