ed chair, not unknown, so the operator must confirm | | | Roihu L40 |","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"beb82d89-7522-4751-b19d-e2104731d845","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies/.claude/worktrees/agent-aef4b903dc16194fa","root":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies/.claude/worktrees/agent-aef4b903dc16194fa","branch":"viktor/viewer-and-val","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":4,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Sairanyx/Newbies","visibility":"unknown"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Sairanyx/Newbies","visibility":"unknown"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Sairanyx/Newbies","visibility":"unknown"}]}},"live_cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies/.claude/worktrees/agent-aef4b903dc16194fa","platform":"linux"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2198adf9-658f-4dde-a377-2000e00b0a9c","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies/.claude/worktrees/agent-aef4b903dc16194fa","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"viktor/fix-copilot-button","slug":"vast-jumping-lobster"}
{"parentUuid":"f018dc1e-6aa6-4b50-80a1-fa4fd1a4b2fa","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3b1f62eb-9e27-45a6-96d8-bf7f61c7cb20","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013vAsiCYCmGbzyEJkHTMnmx","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"best small local LLM CPU only laptop 2026 ollama structured JSON output 2GB 3GB model benchmark tokens per second\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"This metrics tool terrifies bad developers\",\"url\":\"https://www.sitepoint.com/best-local-llm-models-2026/\"},{\"title\":\"DEV Community\",\"url\":\"https://dev.to/studiomeyer_io/local-llms-in-2026-what-actually-works-on-consumer-hardware-50me\"},{\"title\":\"Member-only story\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@mayhemcode/i-spent-two-weeks-finding-the-right-cpu-for-local-llms-heres-what-i-learned-d2a20f1cf195\"},{\"title\":\"LLMs Locally With a CPU? I Tested 8 Models on Linux\",\"url\":\"https://hackernews-dynamic.seasondane.workers.dev/news/48264551\"},{\"title\":\"Can You Run LLMs Locally Without a GPU? I Tested 8 Models on Linux\",\"url\":\"https://itsfoss.com/testing-local-llms-without-gpu\"},{\"title\":\"best local llm models 2026\",\"url\":\"https://pocketllm-landing.pages.dev/blog/best-local-llm-models-2026/\"},{\"title\":\"run llms locally on laptops real limits\",\"url\":\"https://kubaik.github.io/run-llms-locally-on-laptops-real-limits/\"},{\"title\":\"PromptZone - Leading AI Community for Prompt Engineering and AI Enthusiasts\",\"url\":\"https://www.promptzone.com/sloane_pritchard/best-mini-pcs-for-local-llms-in-2026-3kdm\"},{\"title\":\"The 2026 AI Leap: Unveiling the Best SLMs for Your Local Hardware\",\"url\":\"https://networks-hub.pages.dev/slm-edge/2026-ai-leap-slms-local-hardware.html\"},{\"title\":\"PromptZone - Leading AI Community for Prompt Engineering and AI Enthusiasts\",\"url\":\"https://www.promptzone.com/priya_sharma_e952d87d/best-mini-pcs-for-local-llms-in-2026-3kdm\"},{\"title\":\"Beginner 10 minConfiguration\",\"url\":\"https://bestllmfor.com/guide/llm-local-cpu-sans-gpu/\"},{\"title\":\"local llm on laptop\",\"url\":\"https://www.promptquorum.com/local-llms/local-llm-on-laptop\"},{\"title\":\"best cpu only llm\",\"url\":\"https://www.promptquorum.com/local-llms/best-cpu-only-llm\"},{\"title\":\"fastest local llms low end pcs\",\"url\":\"https://www.promptquorum.com/es/local-llms/fastest-local-llms-low-end-pcs\"},{\"title\":\"fastest local llms low end pcs\",\"url\":\"https://www.promptquorum.com/local-llms/fastest-local-llms-low-end-pcs\"},{\"title\":\"Best Mini PCs for Running Local LLMs in 2026\",\"url\":\"https://www.gilricardo.com/blog/best-mini-pc-local-llm-2026\"},{\"title\":\"Benchmark / AI PCs & local LLMs\",\"url\":\"https://verdictbits.com/reviews/ai-pc-benchmark-2026/\"},{\"title\":\"run llm cpu only\",\"url\":\"https://localaimaster.com/blog/run-llm-cpu-only\"},{\"title\":\"Best CPU for LLMs in 2026: What Actually Matters for Local AI Performance\",\"url\":\"https://www.mayhemcode.com/2026/06/best-cpu-for-llms-in-2026-what-actually.html\"}]\n\nI ran one search. It turned up useful tokens-per-second numbers for small CPU-only models, but nothing on structured JSON output, and the sources are mostly low-authority blog and SEO pages.\n\n**Small models on CPU (roughly 2–4 GB)**\n- A PromptQuorum guide dated July 2026 lists Phi-4 Mini (3.8B, about 2.3 GB, 12 tok/s on CPU), Gemma 4 E2B (1.5 GB, 15 tok/s), and Llama 3.2 3B (2 GB, 10 tok/s). The best CPU-only models in July 2026 are Phi-4 Mini (3.8B, ~2.3 GB, 12 tokens/sec on CPU), Gemma 4 E2B (1.5 GB, 15 tokens/sec), and Llama 3.2 3B (2 GB, 10 tokens/sec). A separate PromptQuorum page gives Phi-4-mini 15–25 tok/s, which conflicts with that figure.\n- A different ranking says Llama 3.2 3B fits in ~2 GB at Q4, runs 30+ tok/s on a MacBook Air M2. That is an Apple Silicon result, not x86 CPU-only.\n- An IT's FOSS test reports eval rate of ~25–28 tokens/sec for TinyLlama 1.1B under Ollama on Linux. That is a much smaller model.\n\n**Larger CPU-only reference points**\n- One report says the 9950X does about 11–12 tokens/second on an 8B model according to the LocalScore benchmark. That is a desktop chip, so treat it as an upper bound for laptops.\n- A ThinkPad T14s Gen 3 (Ryzen 7 PRO 6850U, 32 GB) with llama.cpp on CPU reached 8 tokens/sec, 6.5 s per 50 tokens on a 7B Q4_K_M model. That is a closer laptop analogue.\n\n**Memory bandwidth matters most**\n- A CPU-inference write-up notes that a CPU with 90 GB/s memory bandwidth will give you roughly half the tokens per second of a CPU with 180 GB/s bandwidth. For laptop selection, check memory bandwidth and DDR5 support first.\n\n**Gaps**\n- I found no benchmark for structured JSON output (grammar-constrained decoding, schema adherence) or a head-to-head JSON comparison for 2–3 GB models. Those would need a dedicated test, such as Ollama's `format` parameter with a fixed schema, run on your target laptop.\n- The tok/s figures disagree across sources because they use different quantizations, prompt lengths, and thread counts. Treat them as directional and benchmark on your own hardware.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"eca2f4a3-6eba-45b6-8a3d-d06bc8b020db","timestamp":"2026-11-07T14:35:47.352Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"best small local LLM CPU only laptop 2026 ollama structured JSON output 2GB 3GB model benchmark tokens per second","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01PfbQzLB9Xe8ypysPHacjpf","content":[{"title":"This metrics tool terrifies bad developers","url":"https://www.sitepoint.com/best-local-llm-models-2026/"},{"title":"DEV Community","url":"https://dev.to/studiomeyer_io/local-llms-in-2026-what-actually-works-on-consumer-hardware-50me"},{"title":"Member-only story","url":"https://medium.com/@mayhemcode/i-spent-two-weeks-finding-the-right-cpu-for-local-llms-heres-what-i-learned-d2a20f1cf195"},{"title":"LLMs Locally With a CPU? I Tested 8 Models on Linux","u