at-actually.html"}]},"I ran one search. It turned up useful tokens-per-second numbers for small CPU-only models, but nothing on structured JSON output, and the sources are mostly low-authority blog and SEO pages.\n\n**Small models on CPU (roughly 2–4 GB)**\n- A PromptQuorum guide dated July 2026 lists Phi-4 Mini (3.8B, about 2.3 GB, 12 tok/s on CPU), Gemma 4 E2B (1.5 GB, 15 tok/s), and Llama 3.2 3B (2 GB, 10 tok/s). The best CPU-only models in July 2026 are Phi-4 Mini (3.8B, ~2.3 GB, 12 tokens/sec on CPU), Gemma 4 E2B (1.5 GB, 15 tokens/sec), and Llama 3.2 3B (2 GB, 10 tokens/sec). A separate PromptQuorum page gives Phi-4-mini 15–25 tok/s, which conflicts with that figure.\n- A different ranking says Llama 3.2 3B fits in ~2 GB at Q4, runs 30+ tok/s on a MacBook Air M2. That is an Apple Silicon result, not x86 CPU-only.\n- An IT's FOSS test reports eval rate of ~25–28 tokens/sec for TinyLlama 1.1B under Ollama on Linux. That is a much smaller model.\n\n**Larger CPU-only reference points**\n- One report says the 9950X does about 11–12 tokens/second on an 8B model according to the LocalScore benchmark. That is a desktop chip, so treat it as an upper bound for laptops.\n- A ThinkPad T14s Gen 3 (Ryzen 7 PRO 6850U, 32 GB) with llama.cpp on CPU reached 8 tokens/sec, 6.5 s per 50 tokens on a 7B Q4_K_M model. That is a closer laptop analogue.\n\n**Memory bandwidth matters most**\n- A CPU-inference write-up notes that a CPU with 90 GB/s memory bandwidth will give you roughly half the tokens per second of a CPU with 180 GB/s bandwidth. For laptop selection, check memory bandwidth and DDR5 support first.\n\n**Gaps**\n- I found no benchmark for structured JSON output (grammar-constrained decoding, schema adherence) or a head-to-head JSON comparison for 2–3 GB models. Those would need a dedicated test, such as Ollama's `format` parameter with a fixed schema, run on your target laptop.\n- The tok/s figures disagree across sources because they use different quantizations, prompt lengths, and thread counts. Treat them as directional and benchmark on your own hardware."],"durationSeconds":8.31833058000356,"searchCount":1},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"beb82d89-7522-4751-b19d-e2104731d845","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies/.claude/worktrees/agent-aef4b903dc16194fa","root":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies/.claude/worktrees/agent-aef4b903dc16194fa","branch":"viktor/viewer-and-val","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":4,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Sairanyx/Newbies","visibility":"unknown"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Sairanyx/Newbies","visibility":"unknown"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Sairanyx/Newbies","visibility":"unknown"}]}},"live_cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies/.claude/worktrees/agent-aef4b903dc16194fa","platform":"linux"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f018dc1e-6aa6-4b50-80a1-fa4fd1a4b2fa","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_permanent","reasonType":"rule","ruleSource":"userSettings"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies/.claude/worktrees/agent-aef4b903dc16194fa","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"viktor/fix-copilot-button","slug":"vast-jumping-lobster"}
