reToolInputs":{"toolu_013x4Mmb2wDKy7b7tPp3dvqp":{"command":"W=/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies/.claude/worktrees/agent-aef4b903dc16194fa; cd \"$W\"; sed -n 1,16p tests/test_copilot_llm.py | cut -c1-90; grep -n \"^## \" docs/USAGE.md | cut -c1-60; sed -n 5,32p docs/USAGE.md | cut -c1-110; sed -n \"$(grep -n '^## Move an object' docs/USAGE.md | cut -d: -f1),+9p\" docs/USAGE.md | cut -c1-110; sed -n \"$(grep -n '^## Add a missed' docs/USAGE.md | cut -d: -f1),+22p\" docs/USAGE.md | cut -c1-110; sed -n \"$(grep -n '^## Ask the copilot' docs/USAGE.md | cut -d: -f1),+24p\" docs/USAGE.md | cut -c1-110; sed -n \"$(grep -n '^## Copilot voice' docs/USAGE.md | cut -d: -f1),+6p\" docs/USAGE.md | cut -c1-110; grep -n \"make model\" README.md AGENTS.md docs/PLAN.md | cut -c1-110; sed -n 63,66p Makefile | cut -c60-110 | head -0; grep -n \"reload\" Makefile start | cut -c1-90","description":"Read the guide sections that need updating"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"dd5b916e-4e7c-4061-912e-c6d2d479a2f4","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgopC7yz7EwpANmcyhdSF","requestRef":"0f87a5d3-fd35-4d8a-8514-6420b48b04b4","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"535f6131-010e-47a7-a9cc-35ad168d65d3","timestamp":"2026-11-07T15:36:12.708Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies/.claude/worktrees/agent-aef4b903dc16194fa","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"viktor/fix-copilot-button","slug":"vast-jumping-lobster"}
{"parentUuid":"535f6131-010e-47a7-a9cc-35ad168d65d3","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3b1f62eb-9e27-45a6-96d8-bf7f61c7cb20","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013x4Mmb2wDKy7b7tPp3dvqp","type":"tool_result","content":"import json\n\nimport pytest\n\nfrom app.copilot.copilot import CopilotResponse  # noqa: E402\nfrom app.copilot.llm import (  # noqa: E402\n    Fact,\n    check_reply,\n    explain,\n    parse_reply,\n    service_date_note,\n)\n\nFACTS = [\n    Fact(\"ASSET-017\", \"tag: P-005\"),\n    Fact(\"ASSET-017\", \"process flow pct: now 64.557, range 63.347 to 83.191, decreasing.\")\n5:## Set up\n22:## Run it\n37:## Highlight an object's surface\n52:## BIM mode\n77:## Move an object\n116:## Add a missed object\n122:## Split an object that's really two things\n131:## Combine objects that are really one thing\n136:## See the floor layout\n147:## Ask the copilot\n151:## Other controls\n168:## If something's wrong\n191:## Tablet mode\n197:## Control the viewer with commands\n206:## Copilot voice\n## Set up\nYou need `gh auth login` once, plus two files from Viktor that aren't in git:\n- `Equipment Room.ply`, in `data/scene/equipment_room/`\n- The Excel pack, in `data/`, as any `.xlsx` file\n\n```bash\ngit pull\nmake scene      # objects, floor map, and light scenes\nmake mapping    # links Excel records to objects, writes assets_mapped.json\nmake pieces     # cuts movable objects out of the scene\nmake highlights # exports cyan segmented surfaces for object selection\nmake bim        # simulated BIM model for BIM mode, plus model.ifc\nmake db         # optional, needs Docker: keeps changes after a restart\nmake model      # optional, about 20 GB: the copilot's language model\n```\nRun these with internet. The demo itself needs none.\n\n## Run it\n**The short way:** `./start browser` on a laptop or PC, or `./start tablet` for the Lenovo. Each starts the\ndatabase, API, and viewer, and prints the address to open. Ctrl+C stops it. `make start-browser` and\n`make start-tablet` do the same.\n\n**Step by step:** Use two terminals. **Both must run, and both must use the same objects.**\n```bash\nmake api\nmake web SCENE=data/scene/equipment_room/cut/base.ply ASSETS=data/scene/equipment_room/assets_mapped.json SHAP\n```\nOpen http://localhost:8000. On a tablet on the same network, use `http://<this machine's IP>:8000`.\n## Move an object\n1. Tap the object. The smallest box under your finger is selected.\n2. Press **Move on floor**. Only movable objects have this button.\n3. Drag anywhere on the screen. The object follows your drag across the floor.\n4. Release to save. If a route is showing, it plans again.\n   - If the spot is taken, the object and whatever's in its way turn red, and the panel says why.\n   - Releasing on a red spot puts it back at the last good spot. A wall or fixed equipment blocks it too.\n5. **Undo changes** puts everything back.\n\n**Try this first:** the roll cage `obj-0067`. Plan a route with **Go to P-005** from the middle of the room,\n## Add a missed object\n1. Press **Add object**, then drag a box around it or tap it.\n2. Check the orange box. Use **Bigger** or **Smaller** if it's off.\n3. Check the type and whether it can move. A model suggests these if `make model` has run.\n4. Press **Save**. It blocks routes straight away and is marked \"new, unconfirmed\".\n\n## Split an object that's really two things\n1. Tap the object, and press **Split into two**. Objects linked to a record can't be split.\n2. Drag a box around one part. Orange is what you selected, and blue is the rest.\n3. Check the type and whether each can move, then press **Save**. Both are marked \"new, unconfirmed\".\n\nSplit or combine before moving: a moved object has to be put back first, with **Undo changes**.\n\nSet a part to movable to move it, and its real splats go with it. **Undo changes** brings the original back.\n\n## Combine objects that are really one thing\n1. Tap the first object, and press **Combine with...**. Objects linked to a record can't be combined.\n2. Tap the second object. An orange box appears around both.\n3. Check the type and whether it can move, then press **Save**. **Undo changes** brings the originals back.\n\n## See the floor layout\nPress **Plan** for the room from above: walls, objects by type, the route, and an arrow showing where you are.\nColours match BIM mode, and a dashed outline means the object can be moved.\n## Ask the copilot\nSelect an object and press **Ask copilot**, or press **Copilot**. The note under each answer says whether the\nmodel worded it or it's a fixed template. Unsafe requests are refused.\n\n## Other controls\n| Control | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| **Go to P-005** | Plans a route to the faulty device from where you stand. Arrows show the way |\n| **Walk / Fly** | In **Walk** the route starts from wherever you move to. In **Fly** you can look around from\n| **Walk route** | Walks the route, and stops looking at the device |\n| **Person / Robot** | Changes the body size and height for routes |\n| **Plan** | Shows the floor layout from above |\n| **Range** | How far away frames and labels show |\n| **Boxes on** | Shows or hides frames |\n| **Scan / Both / Objects** | The real scan, fitted shapes over it, or shapes only |\n| **BIM** | Simulated BIM model of the room, with IFC properties. Needs `make bim` |\n| **Apart** | Pulls objects apart to show them separately |\n| **Phone** | Turn the device to look, and walk to move. Needs `make web HTTPS=1` |\n\nAdd these to the URL: `?lod=0&res=2` for the sharpest image, or `?res=0.5` if it's slow.\n\n## If something's wrong\n| What you see | Why | Fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| \"Backend not connected\" | `make api` isn't running | Start it. Check http://localhost:8001/docs |\n## Copilot voice\nThe copilot reads its answer aloud with the device's own voice. **Voice on** turns this off. A device with\nno voice installed stays silent. Speaking to it isn't built yet: browser speech recognition usually needs\ninternet, so offline needs a local model such as Whisper.\n\nREADME.md:37:| `make model` | Download the copilot's language model (about 20 GB), before going offline |\nAGENTS.md:89:| `make model` | Get the copilot's language model, before going offline |\nMakefile:74:\tuv run uvicorn app.api.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8001 --reload","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"f2a6fc7f-5a5c-4fb2-a844-26cf1456c7a6","timestamp":"2026-11-07T15:36:13.183Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"import json\n\nimport pytest\n\nfrom app.copilot.copilot import CopilotResponse  # noqa: E402\nfrom app.copilot.llm import (  # noqa: E402\n    Fact,\n    check_reply,\n    explain,\n    parse_reply,\n    service_date_note,\n)\n\nFACTS = [\n    Fact(\"ASSET-017\", \"tag: P-005\"),\n    Fact(\"ASSET-017\", \"process flow pct: now 64.557, range 63.347 to 83.191, decreasing.\")\n5:## Set up\n22:## Run it\n37:## Highlight an object's surface\n52:## BIM mode\n77:## Move an object\n116:## Add a missed object\n122:## Split an object that's really two things\n131:## Combine objects that are really one thing\n136:## See the floor layout\n147:## Ask the copilot\n151:## Other controls\n168:## If something's wrong\n191:## Tablet mode\n197:## Control the viewer with commands\n206:## Copilot voice\n## Set up\nYou need `gh auth login` once, plus two files from Viktor that aren't in git:\n- `Equipment Room.ply`, in `data/scene/equipment_room/`\n- The Excel pack, in `data/`, as any `.xlsx` file\n\n```bash\ngit pull\nmake scene      # objects, floor map, and light scenes\nmake mapping    # links Excel records to objects, writes assets_mapped.json\nmake pieces     # cuts movable objects out of the scene\nmake highlights # exports cyan segmented surfaces for object selection\nmake bim        # simulated BIM model for BIM mode, plus model.ifc\nmake db         # optional, needs Docker: keeps changes after a restart\nmake model      # optional, about 20 GB: the copilot's language model\n```\nRun these with internet. The demo itself needs none.\n\n## Run it\n**The short way:** `./start browser` on a laptop or PC, or `./start tablet` for the Lenovo. Each starts the\ndatabase, API, and viewer, and prints the address to open. Ctrl+C stops it. `make start-browser` and\n`make start-tablet` do the same.\n\n**Step by step:** Use two terminals. **Both must run, and both must use the same objects.**\n```bash\nmake api\nmake web SCENE=data/scene/equipment_room/cut/base.ply ASSETS=data/scene/equipment_room/assets_mapped.json SHAP\n```\nOpen http://localhost:8000. On a tablet on the same network, use `http://<this machine's IP>:8000`.\n## Move an object\n1. Tap the object. The smallest box under your finger is selected.\n2. Press **Move on floor**. Only movable objects have this button.\n3. Drag anywhere on the screen. The object follows your drag across the floor.\n4. Release to save. If a route is showing, it plans again.\n   - If the spot is taken, the object and whatever's in its way turn red, and the panel says why.\n   - Releasing on a red spot puts it back at the last good spot. A wall or fixed equipment blocks it too.\n5. **Undo changes** puts everything back.\n\n**Try this first:** the roll cage `obj-0067`. Plan a route with **Go to P-005** from the middle of the room,\n## Add a missed object\n1. Press **Add object**, then drag a box around it or tap it.\n2. Check the orange box. Use **Bigger** or **Smaller** if it's off.\n3. Check the type and whether it can move. A model suggests these if `make model` has run.\n4. Press **Save**. It blocks routes straight away and is marked \"new, unconfirmed\".\n\n## Split an object that's really two things\n1. Tap the object, and press **Split into two**. Objects linked to a record can't be split.\n2. Drag a box around one part. Orange is what you selected, and blue is the rest.\n3. Check the type and whether each can move, then press **Save**. Both are marked \"new, unconfirmed\".\n\nSplit or combine before moving: a moved object has to be put back first, with **Undo changes**.\n\nSet a part to movable to move it, and its real splats go with it. **Undo changes** brings the original back.\n\n## Combine objects that are really one thing\n1. Tap the first object, and press **Combine with...**. Objects linked to a record can't be combined.\n2. Tap the second object. An orange box appears around both.\n3. Check the type and whether it can move, then press **Save**. **Undo changes** brings the originals back.\n\n## See the floor layout\nPress **Plan** for the room from above: walls, objects by type, the route, and an arrow showing where you are.\nColours match BIM mode, and a dashed outline means the object can be moved.\n## Ask the copilot\nSelect an object and press **Ask copilot**, or press **Copilot**. The note under each answer says whether the\nmodel worded it or it's a fixed template. Unsafe requests are refused.\n\n## Other controls\n| Control | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| **Go to P-005** | Plans a route to the faulty device from where you stand. Arrows show the way |\n| **Walk / Fly** | In **Walk** the route starts from wherever you move to. In **Fly** you can look around from\n| **Walk route** | Walks the route, and stops looking at the device |\n| **Person / Robot** | Changes the body size and height for routes |\n| **Plan** | Shows the floor layout from above |\n| **Range** | How far away frames and labels show |\n| **Boxes on** | Shows or hides frames |\n| **Scan / Both / Objects** | The real scan, fitted shapes over it, or shapes only |\n| **BIM** | Simulated BIM model of the room, with IFC properties. Needs `make bim` |\n| **Apart** | Pulls objects apart to show them separately |\n| **Phone** | Turn the device to look, and walk to move. Needs `make web HTTPS=1` |\n\nAdd these to the URL: `?lod=0&res=2` for the sharpest image, or `?res=0.5` if it's slow.\n\n## If something's wrong\n| What you see | Why | Fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| \"Backend not connected\" | `make api` isn't running | Start it. Check http://localhost:8001/docs |\n## Copilot voice\nThe copilot reads its answer aloud with the device's own voice. **Voice on** turns this off. A device with\nno voice installed stays silent. Speaking to it isn't built yet: browser speech recognition usually needs\ninternet, so offline needs a local model such as Whisper.\n\nREADME.md:37:| `make model` | Download the copilot's language model (about 20 GB), before going offline |\nAGENTS.md:89:| `make model` | Get the copilot's language model, before going offline |\nMakefile:74:\tuv run uvicorn app.api.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8001 --reload","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"dd5b916e-4e7c-4061-912e-c6d2d479a2f4","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies/.claude/worktrees/agent-aef4b903dc16194fa","root":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies/.claude/worktrees/agent-aef4b903dc16194fa","branch":"viktor/viewer-and-val","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":19,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":1},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Sairanyx/Newbies","visibility":"unknown"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Sairanyx/Newbies","visibility":"unknown"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Sairanyx/Newbies","visibility":"unknown"}]}},"live_cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies/.claude/worktrees/agent-aef4b903dc16194fa","platform":"linux"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"535f6131-010e-47a7-a9cc-35ad168d65d3","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies/.claude/worktrees/agent-aef4b903dc16194fa","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"viktor/fix-copilot-button","slug":"vast-jumping-lobster"}
