{"parentUuid":"8019fa9a-0c2e-4851-84c8-6ceb58880aa3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgopCoWmTZqhcsZQCuz5Y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CiSMXoXbbwVZH2zhTejrzN","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"W=/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies/.claude/worktrees/agent-aef4b903dc16194fa; cd \"$W\"; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re\ndef patch(path, pairs):\n    t = open(path).read()\n    for old, new in pairs:\n        assert old in t, (path, old[:80])\n        t = t.replace(old, new, 1)\n    open(path, \"w\").write(t)\npatch(\"docs/USAGE.md\", [\n('''make model      # optional, about 20 GB: the copilot's language model\n''', '''make laptop-model # optional, needs Ollama: Val's small model for a laptop with no GPU\nmake model      # optional, about 20 GB, for a GPU: Val's larger model\n'''),\n('''2. Press **Move on floor**. Only movable objects have this button.\n''', '''2. Press **Move**, or **Rotate** to turn it. Only movable objects have these buttons.\n'''),\n('''5. **Undo changes** puts everything back.\n''', '''5. **Done**, or Esc, finishes. **Undo changes** in **More** puts everything back.\n'''),\n('''## Add a missed object\n1. Press **Add object**, then''', '''## Duplicate or delete an object\nTap an object to find both buttons.\n- **Duplicate** puts a copy on a free spot beside it, with its real splats and type, in the scan and in BIM\n  mode. A copy has no record link: it isn't the same device, so it never shows as `P-005`.\n- **Delete** asks first, then removes the object from the scan, the routes, BIM mode and the exports.\n  **Undo changes** brings it back. It hides the object's whole box, so a neighbour inside it goes too.\n\n## Go back\nEsc, or the back button on a phone, goes back one step: it closes **More**, cancels a question or a selection\nbox, finishes a move, stops a walk, closes Val or Plan, and then deselects the object.\n\n## Add a missed object\n1. In **More**, press **Add object**, then'''),\n('''1. Tap the object, and press **Split into two**. Objects''', '''1. Tap the object, and under **Fix this object** press **Split into two**. Objects'''),\n('''1. Tap the first object, and press **Combine with...**. Objects''', '''1. Tap the first object, and under **Fix this object** press **Combine with...**. Objects'''),\n('''## Ask the copilot\nSelect an object and press **Ask copilot**, or press **Copilot**. The note under each answer says whether the\nmodel worded it or it's a fixed template. Unsafe requests are refused.\n''', '''## Ask Val\nVal is the field-service assistant. Press **Ask Val**, with or without an object selected, then type or tap a\nsuggestion. It can say what needs attention, what's wrong with a device, what to check next and when it was\nlast serviced, and it can take you there by drawing the route. **× ** beside \"About ...\" stops asking about\nthat object.\n\nVal answers from the plant's records straight away. With a language model running, the model's plainer wording\nreplaces that answer when it's ready, which can take a while on a laptop, and only if code's checks pass. **How\nVal knows** shows what's recorded, possible causes, confidence and how it was worded. Val says when it has no\nrecords on something, doesn't guess which device an unlinked object is, and refuses to operate equipment.\n'''),\n('''## Other controls\n| Control | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| **Go to P-005** | Plans a route to the faulty device from where you stand. Arrows show the way |\n| **Walk / Fly** |''', '''## Other controls\nThe main buttons are **Go to P-005**, **Plan**, **Ask Val** and **More**, with **Walk route** and **Clear route**\nwhile a route shows. Everything else is in **More**.\n\n| Control | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| **Go to P-005** | Plans a route to the faulty device from where you stand. Arrows show the way |\n| **Movement: Walk / Fly** |'''),\n('''| **Person / Robot** |''', '''| **Route for: Person / Robot** |'''),\n('''| **Scan / Both / Objects** |''', '''| **View: Scan / Both / Objects** |'''),\n('''Add these to the URL: `?lod=0&res=2` for the sharpest image, or `?res=0.5` if it's slow.\n''', '''## If it's slow\nThe viewer helps itself: it stops redrawing while nothing changes, lowers the resolution while moving if the\ndevice can't keep up and sharpens when you stop, and uses the light scene on anything without a graphics card.\nThese go in the URL:\n- `?res=0.5` draws fewer pixels. `?lod=0&res=2` is the sharpest.\n- `?scene=light` or `?scene=full` chooses the scene.\n- `?adaptive=0` keeps the resolution fixed. `?debug=1` shows the frame rate.\n\nRun `make web` with `LIGHT=$(SCENE_DIR)/light_full.ply` so that the light scene is on offer.\n'''),\n('''## Copilot voice\nThe copilot reads its answer aloud''', '''## Val's voice\nVal reads its answer aloud'''),\n])\nt = open(\"docs/USAGE.md\").read()\nt = t.replace(\"**Ask copilot**, \", \"**Ask Val**, \").replace(\"**Move on floor**\", \"**Move**\").replace(\"so a voice copilot can\", \"so a voice assistant can\")\nopen(\"docs/USAGE.md\", \"w\").write(t)\npatch(\"README.md\", [(\"| `make model` | Download the copilot's language model (about 20 GB), before going offline |\", \"| `make laptop-model` | Get Val's small model for a laptop with no GPU, before going offline. Needs Ollama |\\n| `make model` | Download Val's larger model for a GPU (about 20 GB), before going offline |\")])\npatch(\"AGENTS.md\", [(\"| `make model` | Get the copilot's language model, before going offline |\", \"| `make laptop-model` | Get Val's small model, for a laptop with no GPU |\\n| `make model` | Get Val's larger model, for a GPU, before going offline |\")])\npatch(\"Makefile\", [(\"uvicorn app.api.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8001 --reload\", \"uvicorn app.api.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8001 --reload --reload-dir app\")])\npatch(\"tests/test_copilot_llm.py\", [\n('''    explain,\n''', '''    explain,\n    fewer_facts,\n'''),\n])\nopen(\"tests/test_copilot_llm.py\", \"a\").write('''\n\ndef test_a_reply_of_nothing_but_a_citation_is_rejected():\n    reply = {\"answer\": \"[ASSET-017]\", \"hypotheses\": [], \"citations\": [\"ASSET-017\"]}\n    assert check_reply(reply, FACTS) == \"no answer\"\n    assert check_reply({**reply, \"answer\": \"service_completed\"}, FACTS) == \"no answer\"\n\n\ndef test_fewer_facts_keeps_each_kind_in_a_fixed_order():\n    facts = [Fact(\"ASSET-1\", \"a\"), *(Fact(f\"DQ-{i}\", \"q\") for i in range(10)), Fact(\"WO-1\", \"w\")]\n    kept = fewer_facts(facts, 4)\n    assert [fact.id for fact in kept] == [\"ASSET-1\", \"DQ-0\", \"DQ-1\", \"WO-1\"]\n    assert fewer_facts(facts, 50) == facts\n''')\nopen(\"tests/test_api.py\", \"a\").write('''\n\ndef test_copilot_placeholder_says_val_isnt_connected(client):\n    reply = client.post(\"/api/copilot/query\", json={\"question\": \"hi\", \"quick\": True}).json()\n    assert \"Val\" in reply[\"answer\"] or reply[\"placeholder\"] is False\n''')\nEOF\ngrep -n \"LIGHT\" Makefile | cut -c1-90 | head -3; uv run --only-group dev ruff format tests 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-50; uv run --only-group dev ruff check . 2>&1 | grep -E \"^[A-Z][0-9]+ |All checks\" | cut -c1-80; PYTHONPATH=. uv run --no-project --with numpy --with scipy --with pandas --with openpyxl --with pytest --with fastapi --with httpx --with pillow --with 'psycopg[binary]' pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider tests/test_copilot_llm.py tests/test_api.py 2>&1 | tail -4 | cut -c1-140","description":"Update the guide, add tests and limit the API's auto-restart","timeout":120000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3116,"cache_read_input_tokens":620957,"output_tokens":2999,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3116,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2999,"cache_read_input_tokens":620957,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3116,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3116},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":22688,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01CiSMXoXbbwVZH2zhTejrzN":{"command":"W=/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies/.claude/worktrees/agent-aef4b903dc16194fa; cd \"$W\"; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re\ndef patch(path, pairs):\n    t = open(path).read()\n    for old, new in pairs:\n        assert old in t, (path, old[:80])\n        t = t.replace(old, new, 1)\n    open(path, \"w\").write(t)\npatch(\"docs/USAGE.md\", [\n('''make model      # optional, about 20 GB: the copilot's language model\n''', '''make laptop-model # optional, needs Ollama: Val's small model for a laptop with no GPU\nmake model      # optional, about 20 GB, for a GPU: Val's larger model\n'''),\n('''2. Press **Move on floor**. Only movable objects have this button.\n''', '''2. Press **Move**, or **Rotate** to turn it. Only movable objects have these buttons.\n'''),\n('''5. **Undo changes** puts everything back.\n''', '''5. **Done**, or Esc, finishes. **Undo changes** in **More** puts everything back.\n'''),\n('''## Add a missed object\n1. Press **Add object**, then''', '''## Duplicate or delete an object\nTap an object to find both buttons.\n- **Duplicate** puts a copy on a free spot beside it, with its real splats and type, in the scan and in BIM\n  mode. A copy has no record link: it isn't the same device, so it never shows as `P-005`.\n- **Delete** asks first, then removes the object from the scan, the routes, BIM mode and the exports.\n  **Undo changes** brings it back. It hides the object's whole box, so a neighbour inside it goes too.\n\n## Go back\nEsc, or the back button on a phone, goes back one step: it closes **More**, cancels a question or a selection\nbox, finishes a move, stops a walk, closes Val or Plan, and then deselects the object.\n\n## Add a missed object\n1. In **More**, press **Add object**, then'''),\n('''1. Tap the object, and press **Split into two**. Objects''', '''1. Tap the object, and under **Fix this object** press **Split into two**. Objects'''),\n('''1. Tap the first object, and press **Combine with...**. Objects''', '''1. Tap the first object, and under **Fix this object** press **Combine with...**. Objects'''),\n('''## Ask the copilot\nSelect an object and press **Ask copilot**, or press **Copilot**. The note under each answer says whether the\nmodel worded it or it's a fixed template. Unsafe requests are refused.\n''', '''## Ask Val\nVal is the field-service assistant. Press **Ask Val**, with or without an object selected, then type or tap a\nsuggestion. It can say what needs attention, what's wrong with a device, what to check next and when it was\nlast serviced, and it can take you there by drawing the route. **× ** beside \"About ...\" stops asking about\nthat object.\n\nVal answers from the plant's records straight away. With a language model running, the model's plainer wording\nreplaces that answer when it's ready, which can take a while on a laptop, and only if code's checks pass. **How\nVal knows** shows what's recorded, possible causes, confidence and how it was worded. Val says when it has no\nrecords on something, doesn't guess which device an unlinked object is, and refuses to operate equipment.\n'''),\n('''## Other controls\n| Control | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| **Go to P-005** | Plans a route to the faulty device from where you stand. Arrows show the way |\n| **Walk / Fly** |''', '''## Other controls\nThe main buttons are **Go to P-005**, **Plan**, **Ask Val** and **More**, with **Walk route** and **Clear route**\nwhile a route shows. Everything else is in **More**.\n\n| Control | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| **Go to P-005** | Plans a route to the faulty device from where you stand. Arrows show the way |\n| **Movement: Walk / Fly** |'''),\n('''| **Person / Robot** |''', '''| **Route for: Person / Robot** |'''),\n('''| **Scan / Both / Objects** |''', '''| **View: Scan / Both / Objects** |'''),\n('''Add these to the URL: `?lod=0&res=2` for the sharpest image, or `?res=0.5` if it's slow.\n''', '''## If it's slow\nThe viewer helps itself: it stops redrawing while nothing changes, lowers the resolution while moving if the\ndevice can't keep up and sharpens when you stop, and uses the light scene on anything without a graphics card.\nThese go in the URL:\n- `?res=0.5` draws fewer pixels. `?lod=0&res=2` is the sharpest.\n- `?scene=light` or `?scene=full` chooses the scene.\n- `?adaptive=0` keeps the resolution fixed. `?debug=1` shows the frame rate.\n\nRun `make web` with `LIGHT=$(SCENE_DIR)/light_full.ply` so that the light scene is on offer.\n'''),\n('''## Copilot voice\nThe copilot reads its answer aloud''', '''## Val's voice\nVal reads its answer aloud'''),\n])\nt = open(\"docs/USAGE.md\").read()\nt = t.replace(\"**Ask copilot**, \", \"**Ask Val**, \").replace(\"**Move on floor**\", \"**Move**\").replace(\"so a voice copilot can\", \"so a voice assistant can\")\nopen(\"docs/USAGE.md\", \"w\").write(t)\npatch(\"README.md\", [(\"| `make model` | Download the copilot's language model (about 20 GB), before going offline |\", \"| `make laptop-model` | Get Val's small model for a laptop with no GPU, before going offline. Needs Ollama |\\n| `make model` | Download Val's larger model for a GPU (about 20 GB), before going offline |\")])\npatch(\"AGENTS.md\", [(\"| `make model` | Get the copilot's language model, before going offline |\", \"| `make laptop-model` | Get Val's small model, for a laptop with no GPU |\\n| `make model` | Get Val's larger model, for a GPU, before going offline |\")])\npatch(\"Makefile\", [(\"uvicorn app.api.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8001 --reload\", \"uvicorn app.api.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8001 --reload --reload-dir app\")])\npatch(\"tests/test_copilot_llm.py\", [\n('''    explain,\n''', '''    explain,\n    fewer_facts,\n'''),\n])\nopen(\"tests/test_copilot_llm.py\", \"a\").write('''\n\ndef test_a_reply_of_nothing_but_a_citation_is_rejected():\n    reply = {\"answer\": \"[ASSET-017]\", \"hypotheses\": [], \"citations\": [\"ASSET-017\"]}\n    assert check_reply(reply, FACTS) == \"no answer\"\n    assert check_reply({**reply, \"answer\": \"service_completed\"}, FACTS) == \"no answer\"\n\n\ndef test_fewer_facts_keeps_each_kind_in_a_fixed_order():\n    facts = [Fact(\"ASSET-1\", \"a\"), *(Fact(f\"DQ-{i}\", \"q\") for i in range(10)), Fact(\"WO-1\", \"w\")]\n    kept = fewer_facts(facts, 4)\n    assert [fact.id for fact in kept] == [\"ASSET-1\", \"DQ-0\", \"DQ-1\", \"WO-1\"]\n    assert fewer_facts(facts, 50) == facts\n''')\nopen(\"tests/test_api.py\", \"a\").write('''\n\ndef test_copilot_placeholder_says_val_isnt_connected(client):\n    reply = client.post(\"/api/copilot/query\", json={\"question\": \"hi\", \"quick\": True}).json()\n    assert \"Val\" in reply[\"answer\"] or reply[\"placeholder\"] is False\n''')\nEOF\ngrep -n \"LIGHT\" Makefile | cut -c1-90 | head -3; uv run --only-group dev ruff format tests 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-50; uv run --only-group dev ruff check . 2>&1 | grep -E \"^[A-Z][0-9]+ |All checks\" | cut -c1-80; PYTHONPATH=. uv run --no-project --with numpy --with scipy --with pandas --with openpyxl --with pytest --with fastapi --with httpx --with pillow --with 'psycopg[binary]' pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider tests/test_copilot_llm.py tests/test_api.py 2>&1 | tail -4 | cut -c1-140","description":"Update the guide, add tests and limit the API's auto-restart","timeout":120000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"b1d3edca-ba93-4e51-a85a-1f88f6fe5b0f","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgopCo8hNc6fDxrPaMoWv","requestRef":"2cdc5657-0de3-44b1-99f0-3cfe2967fad8","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCache