{"parentUuid":"786625bb-a1c8-4b78-a998-48be1e813ef8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgoq5xq2t8o5YqeamLQ9v","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JBjaXenfS9hf3MVxfnoihx","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"W=/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies/.claude/worktrees/agent-aef4b903dc16194fa; R=/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies; S=/tmp/claude-1000/-home-viktor-trilar-Projects-Newbies/6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028/scratchpad; cd \"$W\"; python3 - <<'EOF'\nt = open(\"docs/RESULTS.md\").read()\nmarker = \"| 2026-11-07 | Viktor | Moved chair keeps blocking routes\"\nassert marker in t\nrows = (\n\"| 2026-11-07 | Viktor | Viewer frame rate on the demo laptop | Real GPU through Vulkan, headless, 1280 x 800, camera turning, default settings | Main with the full scene against this build, which picks the light scene, lowers resolution while moving and stops redrawing when still | Turning: 13 frames a second on main, 31 here at half resolution, or 26 with the full scene forced. Still: 437 GL draw calls a second on main, 46 here. Load wasn't faster: 9 s on main, 14 to 19 s here, one run each | | | ThinkPad, Ryzen 7 PRO 4750U, integrated graphics |\\n\"\n\"| 2026-11-07 | Viktor | Val's small laptop model, 20 fixed questions, one pass | Excel pack, 12 facts per question through Ollama | `gemma4:e2b`, CPU only | 16 of 20 expectations, 10 model answers of 14 asked for, mean 10.6 s, longest 37 s, safety requests all refused. True in the answers read, but terse and can leave things out, or answer a nearby question: vibration got pressure and flow. So it's shown under the records answer, not instead of it. Two questions each on `llama3.2:3b` and `phi4-mini` gave empty or rejected answers | 149 s | Not measured | ThinkPad, Ryzen 7 PRO 4750U |\\n\"\n)\nopen(\"docs/RESULTS.md\", \"w\").write(t.replace(marker, rows + marker, 1))\nopen(\"handoffs/viktortrilar.md\", \"w\").write(\"\"\"# viktortrilar: viktor/viewer-and-val\n**Goal:** the engineer's feedback: a faster viewer, a simpler UI, and the copilot as Val, running on a ThinkPad\n**Done:** web/pacing.js stops redrawing when still and lowers resolution while moving. `./start laptop` and automatic light scene. Four main buttons plus More, actions first in the panel, Esc and phone back. Val: chat panel, suggestions, overview of what needs attention, instant records answer plus \"In plain words\" from `gemma4:e2b` through Ollama (`make laptop-model`). Delete with confirmation, Duplicate in the viewer and BIM mode. Fixed combine: vanishing chair, ghost chair, chair left in the Box look\n**Verified:** 259 tests passed with the Excel pack, 3 skipped, lint clean. Headless browser on real data: 28 of 28 combine, delete, duplicate and back checks, 66 of 66 route checks, Val with the real model, no page errors. On this ThinkPad's real GPU: 13 to 31 frames a second while turning. Not tested: a person using it, tablet or touch, real phone back button, 5090, `./start laptop` itself\n**Next:** merge #31 then this PR. Try it on the ThinkPad with `./start laptop` and `make laptop-model`. Rehearse\n**Blockers:** merging needs Viktor's word. Load time didn't improve. Gemma's answers are terse. Deleting hides the object's whole box, neighbours included. A moved object's old spot can stay blocked. Live IFC has boxes only. Roihu closed until at least Monday\n\"\"\")\nEOF\nuv run --only-group dev ruff format --check . 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-60; make lint 2>&1 | grep -E \"^[A-Z][0-9]+ |All checks\" | cut -c1-70; (cd \"$R\" && PYTHONPATH=\"$W\" uv run --no-project --with numpy --with scipy --with pandas --with openpyxl --with pytest --with fastapi --with httpx --with pillow --with 'psycopg[binary]' --with ifcopenshell --with ezdxf pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider \"$W/tests\" --rootdir=\"$W\" 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-90); git add -A AGENTS.md Makefile README.md app docs handoffs start tests web; git status --short | grep -v \"^[AM] \" | cut -c1-60; git commit -q -m \"Make the viewer faster and simpler, and bring in Val\n\nSpeed: stop redrawing when nothing changes, lower resolution while moving when\nthe device can't keep up, and use the light scene with no graphics card.\nUI: four main buttons plus More, actions first in the object panel, load\nprogress, messages that fade, and Esc or the phone's back button to go back.\nVal: a chat panel with suggestions, an instant answer from the records, and a\nsmall laptop model through Ollama adding plain words under it. Val also says\nwhat needs attention, and no longer turns unlinked objects into the fault.\nObjects: Delete with a confirmation, and Duplicate in the viewer and BIM mode.\nA copy gets everything except the record link, as it isn't that device.\nCombine: splats stay on screen until the new object has its own, hidden pieces\nstay hidden, and parts no longer stay on in BIM's Box look.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\"; git log --oneline -2 | cut -c1-70; git fetch -q origin; echo \"main moved: $(git rev-list --count HEAD..origin/main)\"; git log --format='%h %an %s' HEAD..origin/main | head -5 | cut -c1-90; git merge-tree --write-tree --name-only origin/main HEAD 2>&1 | sed -n '2,/^$/p' | grep -v '^$' | head | cut -c1-50; gh pr view 31 --json state --jq .state","description":"Record results, run final checks and commit","timeout":200000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2621,"cache_read_input_tokens":648935,"output_tokens":3017,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":814},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2621,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3017,"cache_read_input_tokens":648935,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2621,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2621},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":18983,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01JBjaXenfS9hf3MVxfnoihx":{"command":"W=/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies/.claude/worktrees/agent-aef4b903dc16194fa; R=/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies; S=/tmp/claude-1000/-home-viktor-trilar-Projects-Newbies/6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028/scratchpad; cd \"$W\"; python3 - <<'EOF'\nt = open(\"docs/RESULTS.md\").read()\nmarker = \"| 2026-11-07 | Viktor | Moved chair keeps blocking routes\"\nassert marker in t\nrows = (\n\"| 2026-11-07 | Viktor | Viewer frame rate on the demo laptop | Real GPU through Vulkan, headless, 1280 x 800, camera turning, default settings | Main with the full scene against this build, which picks the light scene, lowers resolution while moving and stops redrawing when still | Turning: 13 frames a second on main, 31 here at half resolution, or 26 with the full scene forced. Still: 437 GL draw calls a second on main, 46 here. Load wasn't faster: 9 s on main, 14 to 19 s here, one run each | | | ThinkPad, Ryzen 7 PRO 4750U, integrated graphics |\\n\"\n\"| 2026-11-07 | Viktor | Val's small laptop model, 20 fixed questions, one pass | Excel pack, 12 facts per question through Ollama | `gemma4:e2b`, CPU only | 16 of 20 expectations, 10 model answers of 14 asked for, mean 10.6 s, longest 37 s, safety requests all refused. True in the answers read, but terse and can leave things out, or answer a nearby question: vibration got pressure and flow. So it's shown under the records answer, not instead of it. Two questions each on `llama3.2:3b` and `phi4-mini` gave empty or rejected answers | 149 s | Not measured | ThinkPad, Ryzen 7 PRO 4750U |\\n\"\n)\nopen(\"docs/RESULTS.md\", \"w\").write(t.replace(marker, rows + marker, 1))\nopen(\"handoffs/viktortrilar.md\", \"w\").write(\"\"\"# v