{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","id":"15fd9829-423a-48c2-b543-839dedd3383e","timestamp":"2026-11-07T15:49:55.461Z","version":"2.1.319","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"722db4f18cedb330133d1505341dd7fba4dc656fa048fe0f251a9d2ff7e226fc","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"4a1f673d-9d90-4435-bfb4-5608f5fb8408","keep":244,"tail":["0b447120b8c90714431c5cbd2e486418f099c1a68733e052cf23a7ae7b3f91cf","41bad599665919cb64058418889a1a0fb2313c98328850d97e42b3c6d0c0bfc2"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",245,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"0fc20bbfc35811f43c24ca8bd1eecba517e4124e45f462a0549d14127d47c0e7"}
{"parentUuid":"68336039-8abb-4f88-9b74-8ec3eae34f9e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgoqFQReVtoX4b8wpci7f","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JsXqVXK52FPwHDim7b8cRZ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"W=/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies/.claude/worktrees/agent-aef4b903dc16194fa; S=/tmp/claude-1000/-home-viktor-trilar-Projects-Newbies/6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028/scratchpad; cd \"$W\"; git push -q git@github.com:Sairanyx/Newbies.git viktor/viewer-and-val 2>&1 | grep -v \"^remote:\" | tail -1 | cut -c1-90; cat > \"$S/pr6.md\" <<'EOF'\nActs on the engineer's feedback: the viewer needs to be much faster and simpler, and the copilot, now named Val, matters most. Runs on a ThinkPad with no 5090. Includes #31.\n\n**Speed, on a ThinkPad's own GPU (Ryzen 7 PRO 4750U, integrated graphics):**\n\n| | Main, full scene | This PR |\n|---|---|---|\n| Frames a second while turning | 13 | 31, at half resolution |\n| GL draw calls a second when still | 437 | 46 |\n| Time to load | 9 s | 14 to 19 s |\n\nOne run each. Load time didn't improve.\n- `web/pacing.js` stops redrawing when nothing changes, lowers resolution while moving if the device can't keep up, and sharpens when you stop.\n- Without a graphics card, the viewer picks the light scene. `./start laptop` cuts objects from that scene.\n- Labels no longer touch the page for all 440 objects on every frame.\n\n**Simpler UI:**\n- Four main buttons (Go to P-005, Plan, Ask Val, More), with route buttons only while a route shows.\n- The object panel leads with actions, and details and fixes are folded away.\n- Load progress bar, messages that fade, and frame rate only with `?debug=1`.\n- Esc or the phone's back button goes back one step.\n- Windows close with their × on tablets too, rather than on any tap.\n\n**Val:**\n- Chat panel with suggestions that fit the selection.\n- New: what needs attention, greetings, and saying plainly when something isn't in the records.\n- \"Take me there\" now draws the route.\n- Fixed: an object with no record could be routed to P-005 instead, and answers could repeat the last device's diagnosis.\n- The answer from the records comes at once. `gemma4:e2b` through Ollama (`make laptop-model`) adds an \"In plain words\" line under it, about 10 s later.\n- The small model's answers were true but terse and sometimes answered a nearby question, so it never replaces the records answer. Llama 3.2 and Phi-4 Mini did worse in a two-question try.\n- The model's prompt is unchanged. Only what the user sees says Val; internal names stay `copilot`.\n\n**Objects:**\n- Delete asks first. It hides the object's whole box in the scan, so a neighbour inside the box goes too. Undo changes brings it back.\n- Duplicate copies an object to a free spot beside it, in the viewer and BIM mode. **A copy doesn't get the record link**, because a second P-005 would be an invented identity.\n\n**Combine bugs fixed:**\n- **Vanishing chair:** the pre-cut piece was hidden, and the new object had no splats until it moved.\n- **Ghost chair:** any view change switched hidden pieces back on.\n- **Chair in BIM's Box look:** BIM's update skipped gone objects, so their splats stayed on.\n\n**Also:** `make api` only restarts on changes in `app/`, so edits in agent worktrees can't wipe moves mid-demo. The viewer's proxy waits 90 s rather than 30 s.\n\n**Tested:**\n- 259 tests passed with the Excel pack, 3 skipped, lint clean. CI skips anything needing numpy.\n- Headless browser on real data with the real Gemma model: 28 of 28 combine, delete, duplicate and back checks on the pre-cut scene, 66 of 66 route checks, and the Val flow. No page errors. The scripts are in a local scratch folder, not this repo.\n- Gemma, 20 fixed questions: 16 of 20 expectations, 10 model answers of 14 asked for, mean 10.6 s, longest 37 s.\n\n**Not tested:** `./start laptop` itself, a tablet or touch, a real phone's back button, the larger model on the 5090, and a person actually using the new layout.\n\n**Known gaps:** the phone back button was only tested through the browser's history. In BIM's Real look, a fixed object is hidden by cutting a box out of a shared file, so neighbours inside the box go too. Eduard's and Benjamin's work is already merged, so anyone with new viewer work should rebase.\n\n**After pulling:** `make laptop-model`, `make bim`, then `./start laptop`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nEOF\ngh pr create --base main --head viktor/viewer-and-val --title \"Make the viewer faster and simpler, and bring in Val\" --body-file \"$S/pr6.md\" 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-80; sleep 8; timeout 150 gh pr checks viktor/viewer-and-val --watch --interval 10 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-70; gh pr view viktor/viewer-and-val --json mergeable,mergeStateStatus,number --jq '\"#\\(.number) \\(.mergeable) \\(.mergeStateStatus)\"'","description":"Push the branch, open the pull request and wait for CI","timeout":220000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3123,"cache_read_input_tokens":651556,"output_tokens":1968,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3123,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1968,"cache_read_input_tokens":651556,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3123,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3123},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":17908,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01JsXqVXK52FPwHDim7b8cRZ":{"command":"W=/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies/.claude/worktrees/agent-aef4b903dc16194f