l's answers were true but terse and sometimes answered a nearby question, so it never replaces the records answer. Llama 3.2 and Phi-4 Mini did worse in a two-question try.\n- The model's prompt is unchanged. Only what the user sees says Val; internal names stay `copilot`.\n\n**Objects:**\n- Delete asks first. It hides the object's whole box in the scan, so a neighbour inside the box goes too. Undo changes brings it back.\n- Duplicate copies an object to a free spot beside it, in the viewer and BIM mode. **A copy doesn't get the record link**, because a second P-005 would be an invented identity.\n\n**Combine bugs fixed:**\n- **Vanishing chair:** the pre-cut piece was hidden, and the new object had no splats until it moved.\n- **Ghost chair:** any view change switched hidden pieces back on.\n- **Chair in BIM's Box look:** BIM's update skipped gone objects, so their splats stayed on.\n\n**Also:** `make api` only restarts on changes in `app/`, so edits in agent worktrees can't wipe moves mid-demo. The viewer's proxy waits 90 s rather than 30 s.\n\n**Tested:**\n- 259 tests passed with the Excel pack, 3 skipped, lint clean. CI skips anything needing numpy.\n- Headless browser on real data with the real Gemma model: 28 of 28 combine, delete, duplicate and back checks on the pre-cut scene, 66 of 66 route checks, and the Val flow. No page errors. The scripts are in a local scratch folder, not this repo.\n- Gemma, 20 fixed questions: 16 of 20 expectations, 10 model answers of 14 asked for, mean 10.6 s, longest 37 s.\n\n**Not tested:** `./start laptop` itself, a tablet or touch, a real phone's back button, the larger model on the 5090, and a person actually using the new layout.\n\n**Known gaps:** the phone back button was only tested through the browser's history. In BIM's Real look, a fixed object is hidden by cutting a box out of a shared file, so neighbours inside the box go too. Eduard's and Benjamin's work is already merged, so anyone with new viewer work should rebase