{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","id":"d14c7e3b-c519-4252-b2b1-5b04c99f0769","timestamp":"2026-11-07T15:50:41.000Z","version":"2.1.319","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"722db4f18cedb330133d1505341dd7fba4dc656fa048fe0f251a9d2ff7e226fc","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"15fd9829-423a-48c2-b543-839dedd3383e","keep":246,"tail":["087f22cacd487f8abaea94e3081b99df13a062e375c4eca6b98fc0c61d8327c0","ceb0e3ec6556f2fd7476263a6869848837e4b5ff8882ffaa407995403d68c180"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",247,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"2c6cbcab65b9abab9c140b80550a6d73e16fc72e2111629d6d031b2760f1575f"}
{"parentUuid":"e92dc601-b413-47cd-97b6-a118bde088d0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgoqJmHcWNmnpZmCX9cmv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Everything you asked for is built and tested, and [#32](https://github.com/Sairanyx/Newbies/pull/32) is ready, but it's not merged yet.** Say \"merge\" and I'll merge it. It includes [#31](https://github.com/Sairanyx/Newbies/pull/31), which fixes a bug my #30 merge brought to main: the Copilot buttons do nothing there right now. Merging #32 fixes that too.\n\nAll the branches are merged into main through #30 (`eduard`, `benjamin/webviewer`, `yasasha/extract`). `hannu_branch` came in with Eduard's. I left out `sasha_branch` (an empty test commit) and `viktor/viewer-objects` (an old merge with no work of its own).\n\n## Speed\nMeasured on this ThinkPad's own graphics chip, one run each:\n\n| | Main, full scene | #32 |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Frames/s while turning** | 13 | 31, at half resolution |\n| **GL draw calls/s when still** | 437 | 46 |\n| **Load time** | 9 s | 14 to 19 s |\n\nThe view gets softer while you move and sharpens when you stop. Load time did not improve. Use `./start laptop` on the ThinkPads, because `./start browser` loads the heavy scene.\n\n## UI\n- **Buttons:** four main ones (**Go to P-005**, **Plan**, **Ask Val**, **More**), down from 16. Everything else is in **More**.\n- **Object panel:** actions come first, and details are folded away.\n- **Back:** Esc or the phone's back button goes back one step.\n- **Delete:** asks first, and **Undo changes** brings the object back. It hides the object's whole box, so anything else inside that box goes too.\n- **Duplicate:** works in the viewer and in BIM mode.\n- **Combine:** the vanishing chair, the ghost chair and the chair showing in BIM's block view are all fixed.\n\n## Val\n- **New answers:** it now says what needs attention, draws the route when you ask to be taken somewhere, and says plainly when the records don't cover something.\n- **Bugs fixed:** \"hi\" used to return a document about control valves, and an object with no record could route you to P-005.\n- **ThinkPad model:** `gemma4:e2b` through Ollama, averaging 10.6 s per answer and 37 s at worst. Llama and Phi returned empty or rejected answers on two test questions.\n- **How answers appear:** the records answer shows instantly, and Gemma adds an \"In plain words\" line under it. I kept both because Gemma's answers were true but thin (\"The issue code is FOULING\").\n\n## Decisions for you\n- **Copies have no record link:** \"exactly the same object\" is true except for this, because a second P-005 would break the rule against inventing identity. Tell me if you'd rather have it copied.\n- **`P-005?` in the demo:** the viewer now shows the question mark in labels and panels, because that link is unconfirmed. **Go to P-005** keeps its name.\n\n## Not tested\n`./start laptop` itself, a tablet or touch, a real phone's back button, the 5090, or a person using the new layout. Please try it yourself after merging, since \"clunky\" is something only you can judge:\n\n```bash\nmake laptop-model   # about 4.6 GB; needs Ollama\nmake bim\n./start laptop\n```\n\nSearch sources I used to pick the candidate models (rough numbers only, so I measured here instead): [PromptQuorum](https://www.promptquorum.com/local-llms/best-cpu-only-llm), [It's FOSS](https://itsfoss.com/testing-local-llms-without-gpu)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2046,"cache_read_input_tokens":654679,"output_tokens":1222,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2046,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1222,"cache_read_input_tokens":654679,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2046,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2046},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"b34f27f0-8c95-415a-9bc3-889e86d38a54","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgoqJkyFwCnCoWB9EZuLm","requestRef":"d14c7e3b-c519-4252-b2b1-5b04c99f0769","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"d2b6f6ad-1d0a-409b-a4ff-1fa411f32d1f","timestamp":"2026-11-07T15:50:52.186Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies/.claude/worktrees/agent-aef4b903dc16194fa","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"viktor/fix-copilot-button","slug":"vast-jumping-lobster"}
